# Cloudflare Pages headers — the security headers previously set in
# apps/web/vercel.json. Vite copies this file verbatim into dist/, where Pages
# reads it. Keep the CSP in sync with any new external hosts the app talks to.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is DEFINED in functions/_middleware.js, which sets it
# on the server-rendered Function routes (_headers never reaches those). Static
# pages no longer run that middleware (see _routes.json: every Function call
# spends the account's daily Workers allowance), so the block below copies the
# same policy here: per host below, and as the first line of the main /* rule
# so a host no rule names still has one. Edit the allow-list in the middleware, then run
# `node scripts/build-app-headers.mjs`; `pnpm run lint` fails if they differ.
# BEGIN app-csp: generated by scripts/build-app-headers.mjs from functions/_middleware.js. Do not edit by hand.
https://app.theplot.tv/*
